# What git must not carry. RepoFiles.txt is the reasoning; this is the part of
# it git can enforce, and the two are meant to agree.
#
# A NOTE ON WHAT .gitignore CANNOT DO, because it cost this project real time:
# it has no effect on a file that is ALREADY TRACKED. Adding a name here does
# not remove it from the repository -- git rm --cached does that, and tidyRepo
# is what runs it. So this file keeps new output out; it does not clean up.
#
# And it cannot sort by what a file is FOR, only by what its name looks like.
# The working material and the documentation set look identical from here:
# both are .md and .htm at the root. That is why notes\ exists -- one folder
# named once below, instead of a pattern that has to judge every future file.

# Working material: saved pages, drafts, retired programs, old copies.
# Kept on disk because it is why several decisions were made the way they
# were, and out of the repository because it is not part of the program.
notes/

# Build output. buildHomerView makes all of it from the sources.
HomerView.exe
HomerView_setup.exe
version.txt
build/
jaws/HomerView.jsb

# Fetched at build time, and large. Named in the setup script so they install,
# but there is no reason to carry a copy of somebody else's library.
Axe.js
Ace.js
Nlp.js

# Third-party programs the installer offers. Downloaded, never authored here.
2htm.exe
pandoc.exe

# Logs. Every script in this project writes one beside itself.
*.log

# What Python leaves behind when a module is imported.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# What Windows and the editors leave behind.
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*~
*.bak

# Untracked by tidyRepo: development files that reached the
# repository through git add -A. They are still on disk.
Announce.docx
HomerView.html
HomerView.jkm
HomerView.jsd
HomerView.jss
HomerViewGlobal.jkm
Hotkeys.ini
Plan.md
build/HomerView.nvda-addon
cleanDir.ps1
installer/license.txt
temp.txt
